              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "While I cannot directly purchase tickets or process payments on your behalf, I can provide all the information and steps you need to book your return (round-trip) train ticket from Boston to New York.\n\nSince today is Sunday, June 7, 2026, **\"next Friday\" will be June 12, 2026.**\n\nHere is everything you need to know to book your trip:\n\n### 1. Key Trip Details to Enter\nWhen booking, you will want to input the following stations:\n*   **Origin:** Boston, MA - South Station (BOS) *(or Back Bay - BBY, depending on which is closer to you)*\n*   **Destination:** New York, NY - Moynihan Train Hall at Penn Station (NYP)\n*   **Ticket Type:** Round Trip (Return)\n*   **Departure Date:** Friday, June 12, 2026\n*   **Return Date:** *[Select your preferred return date, e.g., Friday, June 12 for a same-day return, or Sunday, June 14 for a weekend trip]*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Choose Your Train Service\nAmtrak runs two primary services on this route:\n\n*   **Northeast Regional** (Most popular & budget-friendly)\n    *   **Travel Time:** ~4 hours and 15 minutes\n    *   **Cost:** Typically starts around $31\u2013$70 if booked in advance, but prices rise closer to the departure date. \n    *   **Features:** Coach and Business class, quiet cars, Cafe car, free Wi-Fi, and power outlets.\n*   **Acela** (High-speed & premium)\n    *   **Travel Time:** ~3 hours and 40 minutes\n    *   **Cost:** Usually more expensive (typically $120\u2013$250+ depending on class and demand).\n    *   **Features:** Business and First Class only, faster journey, and highly spacious seating.\n\n---\n\n### 3. How to Book Your Tickets\nYou have a few quick and easy ways to complete your booking:\n\n*   **Online (Recommended):** Go directly to the **[Amtrak Website](https://www.amtrak.com/)** and use the search tool on the homepage. Input your stations and dates to compare times and buy your ticket.\n*   **Mobile App:** Download the official **Amtrak App** on your phone. It is highly convenient because your ticket will download directly to your phone as an eTicket, allowing you to skip station lines and board immediately.\n*   **By Phone:** If you prefer speaking to someone or booking via voice assistant, you can call Amtrak 24/7 at **1-800-USA-RAIL (1-800-872-7245)**.\n\n### Quick Travel Tips\n*   **Book ASAP:** Prices on the Northeast Corridor rise significantly the closer you get to your departure date. Booking today for this coming Friday will secure you the lowest remaining fares.\n*   **Baggage:** Amtrak has a highly generous baggage allowance (you can bring up to two carry-on bags and two personal items for free).\n*   **No Middle Seats:** There are no middle seats on Amtrak, so you will always get either a window or an aisle seat.",
